{"name":"California Peach","hex":"#fcbe6a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"peach","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any tree of species Prunus persica, native to China and now widely cultivated throughout temperate regions, having pink flowers and edible fruit.","Soft juicy stone fruit of the peach tree, having yellow flesh, downy, red-tinted yellow skin, and a deeply sculptured pit or stone containing a single seed."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or pertaining to the color peach.","Particularly pleasing or agreeable."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peach"}],"entries":[{"title":"Production of peaches in California","blocks":[{"text":"California is the largest grower of peaches in the United States, producing about 70% of the total."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Harvesting_and_handling_California_peaches_for_eastern_shipment_%281922%29_%2814597643410%29.jpg/330px-Harvesting_and_handling_California_peaches_for_eastern_shipment_%281922%29_%2814597643410%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Production_of_peaches_in_California","wikidata":"Q115519515"},{"title":"California","blocks":[{"text":"California is a state in the Western United States. It is bordered by Oregon to the north, the Mexican state of Baja California to the south, Nevada to the east, Arizona to the southeast, and the Pacific Ocean to the west. With a population of over 39 million across an area of 163,696 square miles (423,970 km2), it is the most populous U.S. state and the third largest by land area."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Flag_of_California.svg/330px-Flag_of_California.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/California","wikidata":"Q99"},{"title":"Peach","blocks":[{"text":"The peach is a deciduous tree t